<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#owa-obokun">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Owa Obokun</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Owa Obokun is the title of the king of Ijesha, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoruba">Yoruba</a> kingdom in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a> whose capital is Ilesa. Tradition traces the title to the kingdom's founder, linked to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oduduwa">Oduduwa</a> and Ile-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ife">Ife</a>. The Owa Obokun Adimula remains a senior traditional ruler in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osun-state">Osun State</a> today.</p></div>
